{"entries":[{"caption":"Overall survival by treatment arm, stratified by biomarker status. Kaplan–Meier curves for Lev+5FU (orange) versus observation (blue) in biomarker-positive (left; n = 217, 102 events) and biomarker-negative (right; n = 402, 189 events) strata. Shaded bands denote 95% pointwise confidence intervals. Curve separation is visually similar across strata, consistent with subgroup HRs of 0.70 (95% CI 0.48–1.04) and 0.68 (95% CI 0.51–0.91) and a non-significant pre-specified treatment-by-biomarker interaction test (LRT p = 0.89). The wider confidence bands in the biomarker-positive panel reflect the smaller number of events rather than a diminished treatment effect.","key":"fig-km-strat","order":{"section":[4,0,0,0,0,0,0],"number":2}},{"caption":"Overall survival by treatment arm. Kaplan–Meier estimates of overall survival in the full cohort (n = 619; 291 deaths) comparing adjuvant Lev+5FU (orange) versus observation (blue). Shaded bands denote pointwise 95% confidence intervals; the risk table below the curves reports the number of patients still at risk at each timepoint. The Lev+5FU curve lies consistently above the observation curve from approximately one year onward, indicating a sustained survival advantage. This visual separation is consistent with the unadjusted hazard ratio of 0.69 (95% CI 0.55–0.87; p = 0.002) reported in Section Subgroup hazard ratios. Time is expressed in days since enrollment.","key":"fig-km-overall","order":{"section":[3,0,0,0,0,0,0],"number":1}},{"caption":"Forest plot of treatment effect on overall survival by biomarker subgroup. Hazard ratios (HR) for Lev+5FU vs. observation are shown on a logarithmic scale; horizontal lines denote 95% confidence intervals. Point estimates were near-identical across biomarker-positive (HR 0.70) and biomarker-negative (HR 0.68) strata, with overlapping confidence intervals, consistent with the non-significant pre-specified interaction test (LRT p = 0.89). The wider interval in the biomarker-positive subgroup reflects fewer events (102 vs. 189) rather than a smaller treatment effect.","key":"fig-forest","order":{"section":[5,1,0,0,0,0,0],"number":3}}],"headings":["background-and-objective","cohort","overall-kaplanmeier","biomarker-stratified-kaplanmeier","subgroup-hazard-ratios","forest-plot","treatment-biomarker-interaction","limitations-and-discussion","reproducibility","references"]}